We used the same phylogenetic tree generated in RAxML-NG and codon alignment generated in Pal2Nal for each run done in codeml. A run
was done based on the whole phylogenetic tree (One ratio), and invididual runs for each gene selected as the foreground
(Branch-site models with their corresponding nulls). While the phylogenetic tree remains the same, for the branch-site models each
selected foreground gene is marked with #1. Because multiple codeml analysis were done (11 runs) you will see multiple copies of the
Phylogenetic tree file and PalsNal alignment of the soybean DMTase genes. Null folders will be stored inside their corresponding
branch-site model gene folder. The txt file in each analysis is the results.
